{{!
    @template enrol_apply/review_evidence

    The evidence behind the signals: the applicant's comment, the details submitted with the
    application and the earlier applications to the course. A quieter column after the funnel in
    source order; each block carries the id a signal links to.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * commentlabel string - label of the applicant's comment, plain spelling
    * hascomment boolean - whether the applicant wrote one
    * comment string - what the applicant wrote, ALREADY escaped and with its line breaks
      converted by format_text(FORMAT_PLAIN), which is why it is triple stashed
    * nocomment string - what to say when they wrote nothing
    * hassnapshot boolean - whether the applicant submitted any profile detail this reader may see
    * snapshotlabel string - heading of the submitted-details list
    * snapshot array - one entry per submitted field the reader may see, each with the label and
      the value as they were submitted, both the PLAIN spelling and output through double
      stashes. A value can hold newlines, because a textarea custom field is offerable, so the
      cell carries the same white-space rule the report's own free-text cells do
    * hashistory boolean - whether this reader may see earlier applications AND there are any: a
      reader without enrol/apply:viewreports gets no heading at all, since a heading that appears
      only when there is history is itself a disclosure
    * historylabel string - heading of the earlier-applications list
    * history array - one entry per earlier application, each with the date it was submitted and
      the outcome as the report's own formatter words it

    Example context (json):
    {
        "commentlabel": "Comment",
        "hascomment": true,
        "comment": "I would like to join this course.",
        "nocomment": "The applicant did not write anything.",
        "hassnapshot": true,
        "snapshotlabel": "Details submitted with this application",
        "snapshot": [
            {"label": "City/town", "value": "Ouro Preto"},
            {"label": "Registration number", "value": "2026-0042"}
        ],
        "hashistory": true,
        "historylabel": "Earlier applications to this course",
        "history": [
            {"applied": "04/06/26, 11:02", "outcome": "Cancelled"}
        ]
    }
}}
<div class="enrol_apply-evidence">
    <h2 class="h5" id="enrol_apply_review_comment">{{commentlabel}}</h2>
    <div class="enrol_apply-box mb-3">
        {{#hascomment}}{{{comment}}}{{/hascomment}}
        {{^hascomment}}<span class="text-body-secondary">{{nocomment}}</span>{{/hascomment}}
    </div>
    {{#hassnapshot}}
        {{!
            renderer_test scopes its snapshot assertions to this wrapper, because the page shows
            identifying values elsewhere (the identity line). It extracts the panel with a
            non-greedy match up to the first closing div tag, so keep this class first on the div
            and nest no div inside it.
        }}
        <h2 class="h5" id="enrol_apply_review_details">{{snapshotlabel}}</h2>
        <div class="enrol_apply-snapshot enrol_apply-box mb-3">
            <dl class="row mb-0">
                {{#snapshot}}
                    <dt class="col-sm-5 col-lg-12">{{label}}</dt>
                    <dd class="col-sm-7 col-lg-12 enrol_apply-linebreaks">{{value}}</dd>
                {{/snapshot}}
            </dl>
        </div>
    {{/hassnapshot}}
    {{#hashistory}}
        <h2 class="h5" id="enrol_apply_review_history">{{historylabel}}</h2>
        <ul class="enrol_apply-box list-unstyled">
            {{#history}}
                <li class="text-body-secondary">{{applied}} &mdash; {{outcome}}</li>
            {{/history}}
        </ul>
    {{/hashistory}}
</div>
